plaso.tsv: what plaso (the log2timeline/plaso:20260720 Docker image) reads
from the files in tests/fixtures/plaso/ with its windefender_history parser
(psort -o json_line), one line per detection: the file detected, the time
(microseconds since 1970, UTC), the threat's name, the user, the process, the
SHA-256, the container files, the web files and the other resources. Written
from plaso's output, not from this crate.

intrinsec-mplog.tsv: what Intrinsec's mplog_parser (MIT,
https://github.com/Intrinsec/mplog_parser at commit
c8bd1cb96fbb899bccec69f84ff11a346ab16637) reads from
tests/fixtures/written/MPLog-20231219-093000.log (written by gen_mplog.py),
its CSVs converted to UTF-8 and then by intrinsec_tsv.py:

  python3 -m mplog_parser.main -d <dir with the log> -o out
  for f in out/*.csv; do iconv -f UTF-16 -t UTF-8 $f > ${f%.csv}.utf8.csv; done
  python3 -I intrinsec_tsv.py out > intrinsec-mplog.tsv

intrinsec-museum.tsv: the same, run on each DFIRArtifactMuseum protection log
(tests/fixtures/museum/, decompressed, one log per directory), each row
prefixed with the log's path under tests/fixtures/ and a tab.

wddh.tsv: what Orange Cyberdefense's wddh (Apache-2.0,
https://github.com/cert-orangecyberdefense/wddh-parser, version 1.0.1 at commit
0d7ff1efcb21f722f3465cc0a4916d5ab4b5fde2) reads from every detection history
file in tests/fixtures/ (plaso's decompressed first), one line per value: the
file, a key named as this crate names the value (a section and position for
the values whose meaning isn't known), the value. Written by wddh_tsv.py,
which runs the wddh command:

  python3 -I wddh_tsv.py ../fixtures > wddh.tsv
